KG42.register("clusters-d5ff248c2c8ffbe307562ffd",{"id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v142-d-CL002","paper":"23-hierarchical_market_structure","label":"DNO local clearing, pricing and LA awarded-demand transfer","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"DNO local clearing, pricing and LA awarded-demand transfer","market_meaning":"Given bids, demand, capacity bounds and the current import/export inputs, the DNO performs DNEM cost-minimizing clearing and provides awarded results and MCP; the LA submits the awarded DNEM import-side quantity as its WEM bus demand. The current chain also provides partial parameter-preparation rules for single-LA iteration.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM","LEM_DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"General DNEM clearing assumes that distribution lines do not restrict delivery; this does not mean that WEM has no congestion. The parameter branch of R002 is limited to the single-LA algorithm, and the statement about iteration 204 in Case 1 is only a case condition. Demand transfer is connected according to the demand-side role of the import quantity in the WEM balance equation and is not generalized to WEM demand submission of export quantity.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Bid input, DNO allocation, balance-constraint pricing and LA awarded-demand transfer have clear information interfaces and constitute a local clearing and result-delivery rule; the single-LA parameter time-point binding and part of the input generation are not yet closed, and it cannot be claimed that a complete cross-market iteration has been formed.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Bear the local clearing decision, capacity constraints and existing parameter branch, retaining their independent case conditions."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the DNO's pricing responsibility and the correspondence between MCP and the local balance multiplier."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Expresses the LA's responsibility and output interface for transferring the local awarded result as WEM demand."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only references the microgrid bid construction and the correspondence between generation dispatch quantity and clearing input; it does not count as a separate declaration rule."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X-rhom","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta-rho_m","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E000","v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"The microgrid DNEM bid vector is formed in the declaration chain and serves as a price input in the clearing objective; the different local roles of variable and parameter are retained, and it is not asserted on this basis that the two-level model can be solved independently in a one-way sequence."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"The source identifies the DNEM balance multiplier as MCP, and the DNO provides this price; clearing balance and price identification are complementary, not duplicates of the same expression."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::x-P_l_imp","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"The DNO provides the LA's DNEM awarded result, the narrative specifies its WEM demand submission, and the WEM balance equation places the DNEM import quantity on the demand side; only the interface in this direction is established, without adding a submission variable or an equal-quantity constraint."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM001","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X-rhom","v141-c-R002::theta::theta-rho_m"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E000","v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"The definition, together with Eqs. (6) and (19), jointly identifies the same microgrid DNEM bid vector; the operational quantity on the declaration side and the input parameter on the clearing side are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM002","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X-Pm","v141-c-R002::x::x-P_m"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E000","v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g01-E017"],"rationale":"Under the same DNEM model and policy definition, both objects refer to the generation dispatch quantity of microgrid m, used respectively for bid construction and lower-level awarding; local uses and definitions are retained, and it is not presumed that the values are the same under different policies or iterations."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM003","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"Both refer to the DNO bearing the same DNEM clearing and price-providing responsibility; the representative selection is only for display, and all original references are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM004","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R007::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005","v141-b-g01-E015"],"rationale":"The awarded source referenced by R007 is precisely the DNEM clearing activity in R002; this activity is displayed uniformly, without merging the subsequent responsibilities of each chain."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G001","category":"math_incomplete","description":"No explicit time-point binding is established between R002's current import upper limit and export quantity and the general clearing parameters; the v used in the reference index is not registered as a parameter, and the price reused by the branch from step (48) is also not included. The existing branches are insufficient to close an executable iteration.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta-P_l_imp_upper","v141-c-R002::theta::theta-P_l_exp","v141-c-R002::theta::theta-P_l_imp_upper_k","v141-c-R002::theta::theta-P_l_exp_k","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E025","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g02-E13"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"The upstream should supplement observability and index definitions, the binding from current parameters to clearing input, and the related price updates; mathematical relations must not be fabricated in D from narrative order."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G002","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The LA bid required for clearing is retained as input, but its role-1 bid construction has not formed the supplied C chain; R007 also lacks an independent submission quantity or a complete WEM receiving-clearing chain. The shared R001 only supplements the microgrid bid and cannot cover these interfaces.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta-rho_l","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005","v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E013"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"The upstream should supplement role-1 bids and the necessary expressions on the WEM receiving side; at this stage the LA bid is treated as an externally given input, and only source-supported procedural interfaces are retained."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G003","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"pricing.local in R002 and its case-condition binding involve the WEM bus LMP, whereas the node of the same name in R004 explicitly denotes the DNEM MCP; the same node ID is insufficient to prove that these price scopes are consistent, so no same-node representative merging was performed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g03-e05"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g03-wholesale-lmp"],"required_work":"Manually verify C's price attribution and the WEM LMP proposal; keep the current graph frozen, and do not rename WEM LMP as DNEM MCP."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G004","category":"unverified_source","description":"The basis for clearing, multiplier pricing, demand propagation, and algorithm branching is all experimentally permitted unverified B evidence, and has not undergone independent source-text audit or independent C2 review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005","v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g01-E015","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the formulas, bus demand direction, and iteration parameter ranges; the candidate mappings must not be treated as having confirmed source or mathematical correctness."}]},"rule_refs":["23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R002","23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R004","23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R007","23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R001"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-234e316a4df6b1c7","COMP-24f3cdbef9d7cdff","KG31-42e78591f3f99231","KG31-589dd70d32471060","KG40-45833afd23977831"]});
